# Auth and users (this sprint is done)

Identity is implemented. Do not re-open this design unless a new PRD says so.
Source of truth: `ai-workspace/register-login-logout_prd.md`.

## What exists

- D1 `users` table. Public type `User` has no password hash.
- Client hashes with `hashPassword` in `src/lib/password.ts` (SHA-256 hex).
- POST `/api/auth/register` (201), `/api/auth/login` (200), `/api/auth/logout` (200 `{ ok: true }`).
- Bodies send `passwordHash` only. A `password` field is a 400.
- Login identifier is **username**, not email. Username and email may be the same value.
- `/mcqs` is an ungated stub. Logout does not revoke anything server-side.

## Do not add without a new PRD

- Social login, JWT/tokens, cookies, `Set-Cookie`, server sessions, route guards
- Password reset, MFA, roles, email verification
- Changing SHA-256 to bcrypt/Argon2 (teaching baseline; replace only when scoped)
- Importing `src/lib/db.ts` or `user-service.ts` into a `'use client'` file

## When adding MCQs

- New tables go in a new migration. Foreign-key `users.id`.
- Keep prepared statements and numbered placeholders (`?1`, `?2`).
- Mock `@/lib/db` in unit tests. Do not hit real D1. Do not add
  `@cloudflare/vitest-pool-workers` without asking.
- `npm test` is already wired. Write tests first.

## Login 401

Unknown user and hash mismatch both return exactly `"Invalid username or password."`
Login still runs a hash compare when the user is missing (dummy `"0".repeat(64)`) so
timing is less of a tell.
